# Story 52: Symbol Search & Code Intelligence (40s)
# Hook: Ask where something is defined -- symbol_search and tree map your code instantly.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-052-symbol-search-code-intelligence.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 6

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
Ask where something is defined -- symbol_search and tree map your code instantly.

[00:03.0 --> 00:08.0]
Launch rysh inside a codebase you want to understand.

[00:08.0 --> 00:13.0]
Double-press Escape to talk to the agent.

[00:13.0 --> 00:30.0]
Ask where a function or type lives. The agent uses symbol_search to find declarations -- functions, types, methods -- and tree to show the directory structure around it. Both are read-only, so they run without approval.

[00:30.0 --> 00:37.0]
Instead of grepping by hand, you just ask. Code intelligence tools turn a vague question into a precise file and line, with the surrounding structure.

[00:37.0 --> 00:40.0]
Find any declaration, understand any tree -- conversationally.

